architecture-audit/cycle-018-domain-realization-context-boundary/validation/reviewer-wave018-entry.stdout:43:The domain has already started the right vocabulary for 2D realization with `ProjectionElementRealizationContext` (`frontend/src/domain/world/projectionPlane/ProjectionPlaneContext.ts:9`, `frontend/src/domain/world/projectionPlane/ProjectionPlaneContext.ts:20`), and `Element2D.realize2D(context: ProjectionElementRealizationContext)` now uses that type (`frontend/src/domain/world/Element2D.ts:1`, `frontend/src/domain/world/Element2D.ts:108`). The remaining central weakness is that 3D realization and plane-equation contracts still use concrete `World` or `any`: `Element3D.realize3D(world: any): any` (`frontend/src/domain/world/Element3D.ts:40`), `Point3D`/`Line3D`/`Segment3D` import `World` for realization (`frontend/src/domain/world/Point3D.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/world/Line3D.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/world/Segment3D.ts`), and `Plane` uses `any` in plane-equation/realization APIs (`frontend/src/domain/world/Plane.ts`). Static scans in `architecture-audit/cycle-018-wave-plan-extension/static-realization-world-scan.stdout` and `static-any-scan.stdout` capture the current residual seams.
